      {
        "question": "what happens if a payment fails?",
        "answer": "If a payment method fails, Meta suspends outbound messaging from your phone number, and you receive an email alert from Meta. You must then update the payment method and clear any outstanding balance.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "page": 2,
            "text": "Meta bills you directly for every template message delivered through the WhatsApp \nBusiness API. Without a valid payment method on file, your phone numbers may be \ndeactivated and you will be unable to send or receive messages. This applies even if you \nare using WeNext \u2014 Meta\u2019s charges come directly to you, not through WeNext. \n3.2  How do I add a payment method in Meta? \n5.Log in to business.facebook.com \n6.Go to Settings > Payment Settings \n7.Click \u201cAdd Payment Method\u201d \n8.Select your country (India), choose credit or debit card \n9.Enter card details and click Save \n3.3  What happens if my payment method fails? \n\u2022Meta suspends outbound messaging from your phone number \n\u2022You receive an email alert from Meta \n\u2022You must update the payment method and clear any outstanding balance"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "if Meta requires additional review. Indian businesses with GST certificates usually get approved \nfaster. \n2.4  What happens if verification is rejected? \n\u2022Meta sends an email explaining the reason \n\u2022You can resubmit with corrected documents immediately \n\u2022Common rejection reasons: name mismatch, document too old (must be within 6 \nmonths), document not in English (add a certified translation) \n2.5  Do I need verification to start testing? \nNo. Without verification, your account operates at Tier 0 and can send up to 250 messages per \nday to any WhatsApp number. This is sufficient for testing. However, you cannot send OTP/\nauthentication templates and cannot scale beyond 250 messages without completing \nverification. \n3. Payment Method \u2014 Why It Is Mandatory"
          },
          {
            "page": 5,
            "text": "\u2022Template body is identical to an existing approved template \n\u2022Language mismatch \u2014 the selected language does not match the actual content \n\u2022Content about alcohol, tobacco, or pharmaceuticals without proper disclaimers \n5.6  Can I edit a template after submission? \nNo. Templates cannot be edited after submission or after they have been sent. If you need to \nchange content, you must delete the template and create a new one. Deleted templates cannot \nbe recreated with the same name for 30 days. \n5.7  What is template pacing? \nNew templates are not sent to all recipients immediately. Meta first delivers them to a small \ngroup (around 1,000 users) and monitors quality signals (blocks, reports, engagement). Only if"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "2.1  What is Business Verification? \nBusiness Verification is Meta\u2019s process of confirming that your business is a legitimate, \nregistered entity. It is mandatory to unlock higher messaging tiers, send certain template \ncategories, and use authentication templates (OTPs). \n2.2  What documents does Meta accept for verification? \n\u2022GST registration certificate \n\u2022Certificate of Incorporation \n\u2022Business license or trade license \n\u2022Utility bill in the business name (electricity, phone, water) \n\u2022Bank statement showing business name \n2.3  How long does verification take? \nTypically 2\u20135 business days. It can take up to 14 days if documents are unclear, incomplete, or \nif Meta requires additional review. Indian businesses with GST certificates usually get approved \nfaster."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "What is a message template and why do I need one?",
        "answer": "I don't know. The context doesn't explicitly define what a message template is or its purpose beyond needing at least one approved template and sending 500 delivered messages across templates before activating flows.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "page": 0,
            "text": "WeNext.ai\nMeta & WhatsApp Business Platform\nComplete FAQ for Clients  \u2014  Updated March 2026\n1. Meta Business Manager Setup \n1.1  What is Meta Business Manager and why do I need it? \nMeta Business Manager (now called Meta Business Portfolio) is your central hub for all \nMeta assets \u2014 your Facebook Page, WhatsApp Business Account (WABA), ad accounts, \nand payment methods. You cannot connect to the WhatsApp Business API without an \nactive, verified Business Manager. \n1.2  How do I create a Meta Business Manager? \n1.Go to business.facebook.com and click \u201cCreate Account\u201d \n2.Enter your business name, your name, and business email \n3.Add your Facebook Page to the Business Manager \n4.Complete Business Verification (see Section 2)"
          },
          {
            "page": 9,
            "text": "delivered messages across your templates before activating flows. This gives your \naccount the messaging history and quality signal Meta requires. \nQ: Can I use a virtual or VoIP number for WhatsApp API? \nA: Yes, as long as the number can receive an SMS or voice call during the one-time OTP \nverification process. After verification, the number does not need to receive calls. \nQ: What happens if a user blocks my number? \nA: That user can no longer receive your messages. Meta also records the block as a \nnegative quality signal. Too many blocks lower your quality rating and prevent tier \nupgrades. This is why sending relevant, opted-in messages is critical. \nQ: Is there a free tier for WhatsApp API? \nA: There is no traditional free tier, but you get free messaging in specific windows:"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "authentication templates and cannot scale beyond 250 messages without completing \nverification. \n3. Payment Method \u2014 Why It Is Mandatory \n3.1  Why does Meta require a payment method? \nTip: Your business name on the document must exactly match the name you enter in Business \nManager. Even minor mismatches (e.g., \u201cPvt Ltd\u201d vs \u201cPrivate Limited\u201d) cause rejection.\nWeNext.ai  |  Meta & WhatsApp Business FAQ  |  Page 2"
          },
          {
            "page": 9,
            "text": "A: Yes. The number used for WhatsApp API cannot simultaneously be active on the \nWhatsApp personal app or WhatsApp Business app. If you want to use your existing \nnumber, it must be migrated off the app first. \nQ: My Business Verification was rejected. What do I do? \nA: Check the rejection email from Meta for the specific reason. Common fixes: ensure the \nbusiness name matches exactly, use a recent document (within 6 months), provide a \ntranslation if the document is not in English, and resubmit. WeNext support can assist \nyou in preparing the correct documents. \nQ: How many templates do I need before activating WeNext flows? \nA: You need at least 1 approved template, but we recommend sending at least 500 \ndelivered messages across your templates before activating flows. This gives your"
          }
