      {
        "question": "How does automatic tier upgrade work?",
        "answer": "Automatic tier upgrade works as follows: Once you reach Tier 1 (2,000), Meta evaluates your account every 6 hours for upgrade eligibility. To qualify for the next tier, you must have: \n1. A quality rating of Medium or High across all templates and phone numbers, and \n2. Used at least 50% of your current daily limit in the past 7 days. \nIf both conditions are met, Meta upgrades your tier within 6 hours.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "page": 3,
            "text": "4.2  How do I move from Tier 0 (250 messages) to Tier 1 (2,000)? \nYou need to complete ONE of the following: \n\u2022Complete Business Verification in Meta Business Manager, OR \n\u2022Send 2,000 delivered messages to unique users within 30 days using high-quality \ntemplates, OR \n\u2022Have WeNext (as your solution provider) verify your business on your behalf \n4.3  How does automatic tier upgrade work? \nOnce you reach Tier 1 (2,000), Meta automatically evaluates your account every 6 hours for \nupgrade eligibility. To qualify for the next tier: \n\u2022Your quality rating must be Medium or High across all templates and phone numbers \n\u2022You must have used at least 50% of your current daily limit in the past 7 days \n\u2022If both conditions are met, Meta upgrades your tier within 6 hours"
          },
          {
            "page": 3,
            "text": "\u2022You must have used at least 50% of your current daily limit in the past 7 days \n\u2022If both conditions are met, Meta upgrades your tier within 6 hours \n4.4  Can my tier be downgraded? \nNo. As of October 2025, Meta removed automatic tier downgrades. Your quality rating dropping \nto Low will prevent further upgrades but will not reduce your existing tier. Once you reach a tier, \nyou stay there. \nTier Daily Limit Requirement Auto-upgrade\nTier 0 250 messages No verification No\nTier 1 2,000 messages Business verified Yes\nTier 2 10,000 messages 50% usage in 7 days Every 6 hrs\nTier 3 100,000 messages 50% usage in 7 days Every 6 hrs\nUnlimited Unlimited 50% usage in 7 days Every 6 hrs\nNew in October 2025: Limits now apply at the Business Portfolio level, not per phone number. New"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "2.1  What is Business Verification? \nBusiness Verification is Meta\u2019s process of confirming that your business is a legitimate, \nregistered entity. It is mandatory to unlock higher messaging tiers, send certain template \ncategories, and use authentication templates (OTPs). \n2.2  What documents does Meta accept for verification? \n\u2022GST registration certificate \n\u2022Certificate of Incorporation \n\u2022Business license or trade license \n\u2022Utility bill in the business name (electricity, phone, water) \n\u2022Bank statement showing business name \n2.3  How long does verification take? \nTypically 2\u20135 business days. It can take up to 14 days if documents are unclear, incomplete, or \nif Meta requires additional review. Indian businesses with GST certificates usually get approved \nfaster."
          },
          {
            "page": 4,
            "text": "4.5  What is a quality rating and how is it determined? \nYour quality rating (High / Medium / Low) reflects how recipients respond to your messages in \nthe past 7 days. It drops when users block your number, report your messages as spam, or \nignore them repeatedly. It is checked at the Business Portfolio level since October 2025. \n\u2022High quality: Few blocks/reports, good engagement \n\u2022Medium quality: Moderate blocks, some reports \n\u2022Low quality: High blocks/reports \u2014 upgrade eligibility is paused \n5. Message Templates \u2014 Rules & Approval \n5.1  What is a message template and why do I need one? \nA message template is a pre-approved message format that allows businesses to initiate \nconversations with WhatsApp users outside of a customer service window. You cannot"
          }
