        "question": "give me about pricing summary",
        "answer": "Meta charges per message, not per conversation. Key pricing rules include: \n- Service messages (replies within 24 hrs of user-initiated message) are free\n- Utility templates sent within an open 24-hour customer service window are free\n- Templates sent within a 72-hour CTWA/FEP window are free\n- Pricing varies by recipient's country code, with examples including \u20b90.90/message in India and \u20b911.50/message in Germany.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "page": 8,
            "text": "9. Pricing Summary (2026) \nMeta switched from per-conversation billing to per-message billing in July 2025. You are \nnow charged for each individual template message delivered, not per 24-hour \nconversation window. \nKey pricing rules to know: \n\u2022Service messages (replies within 24 hrs of user-initiated message) are always free \n\u2022Utility templates sent within an open 24-hour customer service window are free \n\u2022All templates sent within a 72-hour CTWA/FEP window are free (biggest cost saver) \n\u2022Marketing messages to US numbers (+1) are currently paused by Meta (since April \n2025) \n\u2022Pricing varies by recipient\u2019s country code \u2014 not your business location \n\u2022India marketing messages cost approximately \u20b90.90/message; Germany costs ~\u20b911.50/\nmessage \n10. Frequently Asked Questions"
          },
          {
            "page": 4,
            "text": "conversations with WhatsApp users outside of a customer service window. You cannot \nsend any outbound business-initiated message without an approved template. Templates \nmust be approved by Meta before use. \n5.2  How many templates can I have? \n\u2022Without an approved display name: up to 250 templates per WABA \n\u2022With an approved display name linked to a verified business: up to 6,000 templates per \nWABA \n5.3  What are the template categories? \nMeta organises templates into four categories, each with different pricing and rules: \nPractical note: Most businesses operate comfortably within 250 templates. Focus on getting your core \ntemplates approved first (welcome, cart recovery, order confirmation) before worrying about the limit.\nCategory Cost (India) Free when? Example"
          },
          {
            "page": 5,
            "text": "Pricing note: Rates shown are approximate for India recipients. Exact rates depend on the recipient\u2019s \ncountry code, not your business location. Meta switched from per-conversation to per-message billing \nin July 2025.\n\u2fa0 Important: Always test new templates with a small warm audience before running large campaigns. \nA bad template can block your send queue for your entire contact list.\nWeNext.ai  |  Meta & WhatsApp Business FAQ  |  Page 6"
          },
          {
            "page": 8,
            "text": "\u2022India marketing messages cost approximately \u20b90.90/message; Germany costs ~\u20b911.50/\nmessage \n10. Frequently Asked Questions \nQ: Can WeNext send templates on my behalf without me adding a payment method? \nA: No. Meta bills your WhatsApp Business Account directly. WeNext has no ability to pay \nMeta on your behalf or bypass this requirement. Your payment method in Meta Business \nManager must be active before any templates can be sent. \nQ: Do I need a separate phone number for WhatsApp API? \nWeNext tip: Structure your campaigns to maximise free messaging windows. Run CTWA ads on Meta \nto open 72-hour free windows, then send your marketing templates within that window at zero Meta \ncost.\nWeNext.ai  |  Meta & WhatsApp Business FAQ  |  Page 9"
          }
