          {
            "page": 7,
            "text": "Your display name is what WhatsApp users see as your business name in conversations. It \nmust comply with Meta\u2019s naming guidelines: it must clearly represent your business, cannot be \na generic term, and must not be misleading. Display name approval requires Business \nVerification to be complete first. \n7.4  What is the Official Business Account (green tick)? \nThe green tick (OBA status) is a verification badge that appears next to your business name in \nWhatsApp conversations. It is not automatic \u2014 Meta grants it selectively to well-known brands. \nRequirements include: Business Verification complete, display name approved, consistent high \nquality rating, and significant organic WhatsApp presence. WeNext can help you apply but \napproval is at Meta\u2019s sole discretion."
          },
          {
            "page": 6,
            "text": "6.2  What is the minimum activity required? \n\u2022At least 1 approved template in your WABA \n\u2022Minimum template sends to real users to establish a quality signal (Meta does not \npublish an exact number but WeNext recommends at least 500 delivered messages) \n\u2022Quality rating must be Medium or High \n\u2022Business Verification must be complete \n\u2022Payment method must be active \n6.3  What is a free entry point (FEP) and how does it help? \nA Free Entry Point is when a user initiates a conversation with your business via a Click-to-\nWhatsApp (CTWA) ad on Facebook or Instagram, or via a WhatsApp button on your Facebook \nPage. When this happens: \n\u2022A 72-hour messaging window opens \n\u2022All template messages sent within this window are free (no Meta charges)"
          },
          {
            "page": 4,
            "text": "4.5  What is a quality rating and how is it determined? \nYour quality rating (High / Medium / Low) reflects how recipients respond to your messages in \nthe past 7 days. It drops when users block your number, report your messages as spam, or \nignore them repeatedly. It is checked at the Business Portfolio level since October 2025. \n\u2022High quality: Few blocks/reports, good engagement \n\u2022Medium quality: Moderate blocks, some reports \n\u2022Low quality: High blocks/reports \u2014 upgrade eligibility is paused \n5. Message Templates \u2014 Rules & Approval \n5.1  What is a message template and why do I need one? \nA message template is a pre-approved message format that allows businesses to initiate \nconversations with WhatsApp users outside of a customer service window. You cannot"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "2.1  What is Business Verification? \nBusiness Verification is Meta\u2019s process of confirming that your business is a legitimate, \nregistered entity. It is mandatory to unlock higher messaging tiers, send certain template \ncategories, and use authentication templates (OTPs). \n2.2  What documents does Meta accept for verification? \n\u2022GST registration certificate \n\u2022Certificate of Incorporation \n\u2022Business license or trade license \n\u2022Utility bill in the business name (electricity, phone, water) \n\u2022Bank statement showing business name \n2.3  How long does verification take? \nTypically 2\u20135 business days. It can take up to 14 days if documents are unclear, incomplete, or \nif Meta requires additional review. Indian businesses with GST certificates usually get approved \nfaster."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "question": "Can WeNext send templates on my behalf without me adding a payment method?",
        "answer": "No, WeNext cannot send templates on your behalf without you adding a payment method. According to the context, Meta bills you directly for every template message delivered through the WhatsApp Business API and requires a valid payment method on file. Without it, your phone numbers may be deactivated and you will be unable to send or receive messages, even if you are using WeNext.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "page": 2,
            "text": "Meta bills you directly for every template message delivered through the WhatsApp \nBusiness API. Without a valid payment method on file, your phone numbers may be \ndeactivated and you will be unable to send or receive messages. This applies even if you \nare using WeNext \u2014 Meta\u2019s charges come directly to you, not through WeNext. \n3.2  How do I add a payment method in Meta? \n5.Log in to business.facebook.com \n6.Go to Settings > Payment Settings \n7.Click \u201cAdd Payment Method\u201d \n8.Select your country (India), choose credit or debit card \n9.Enter card details and click Save \n3.3  What happens if my payment method fails? \n\u2022Meta suspends outbound messaging from your phone number \n\u2022You receive an email alert from Meta \n\u2022You must update the payment method and clear any outstanding balance"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "authentication templates and cannot scale beyond 250 messages without completing \nverification. \n3. Payment Method \u2014 Why It Is Mandatory \n3.1  Why does Meta require a payment method? \nTip: Your business name on the document must exactly match the name you enter in Business \nManager. Even minor mismatches (e.g., \u201cPvt Ltd\u201d vs \u201cPrivate Limited\u201d) cause rejection.\nWeNext.ai  |  Meta & WhatsApp Business FAQ  |  Page 2"
          },
          {
            "page": 6,
            "text": "7.2  Can I use my existing WhatsApp Business App number? \nYes, but you must migrate it. The number must be disconnected from the WhatsApp Business \nApp before it can be registered on the API. This process deletes your WhatsApp Business App \nhistory on that number. WeNext can guide you through the migration process. \n7.3  What is a display name and how is it approved? \nWeNext guidance: We recommend clients run a simple utility or authentication template campaign to \n500\u20131,000 contacts before attempting to activate Flows. This ensures your account has the quality \nhistory Meta needs.\nCTWA advantage: This is the biggest cost lever for WeNext clients running CTWA ads. Messages \nwithin the 72-hour FEP window are completely free of Meta\u2019s per-message charges."
          },
          {
            "page": 7,
            "text": "quality rating, and significant organic WhatsApp presence. WeNext can help you apply but \napproval is at Meta\u2019s sole discretion. \n8. Common Blockers & How to Resolve Them \n\u2fa0 Important: Your messaging limit must reach Tier 1 (2,000) before your display name can be \napproved. Complete verification and send your first batch of templates before expecting display name \napproval.\nBlocker Cause Fix\nCannot send templates No payment method on file Add card in Meta Business \nManager > Payment Settings\nStuck at 250 msgs/day Business not verified (Tier 0) Submit documents for Business \nVerification\nTemplate rejected Policy violation or placeholder-\nonly body\nRevise content, add fixed text, \nresubmit\nCannot activate Flows No messaging history / low \nquality\nSend 500+ templates, maintain"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "pdf_names": [
      "WeNext_Meta_WhatsApp_FAQ.pdf"
    ]
  },
