  "0773de59-177d-4d13-b82e-94a6cf20068d": {
    "pdf_name": "Getting_Started_Dashboard_Overview (1).pdf",
    "created_at": "2026-07-18T00:28:15.493781",
    "chat_history": [
      {
        "question": "what is this pdf about explian?",
        "answer": "This document appears to be about WeNext.ai Automations, a tool that helps users streamline their workflow and engage with customers effortlessly. It provides a guide on how to create boards, set up automations, and build flows using various nodes and operations.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "page": 8,
            "text": "- Tag Color: Choose a color to visually identify this tag. \n- Description (Optional): Add any notes or details about this tag. \n[Create/Save Tag]. \n \n \n====================================================================== \n== \n8. AUTOMATIONS \n====================================================================== \n== \n \nAutomations \n \nWeNext.ai Automations help you streamline your workflow and engage with \ncustomers effortlessly. Within Automations, you have several options: \n- WhatsApp Automations \u2014 Send automated messages to customers on \nWhatsApp based on triggers or schedules. \n- WhatsApp Flow \u2014 Create interactive WhatsApp conversations to guide \ncustomers or collect information. \n- Form Submission \u2014 Automate actions triggered when a customer submits"
          },
          {
            "page": 7,
            "text": "Step 1: Open Create Board \n- Navigate to the Boards or Pipeline section. \n- Click on \"Create New Board\" to open the setup window. \n \nStep 2: Enter Board Details \n1. Board Name \n- Field to enter the name of the board. \n- Example: Sales Pipeline \n- This name will be used to identify the board in the system. \n2. Description \n- Add a short explanation of the board's purpose. \n- Example: Track potential deals \n- Helps users understand what the board is used for. \n3. Linked Automation (Optional) \n- Dropdown menu to select an automation flow. \n- This links the board with an existing automation for easier task or \nworkflow management. \n- This step is optional and can be skipped if no automation is needed. \n \nStep 3: Complete or Cancel \n1. Create Board \u2014 Click to save and create the board."
          },
          {
            "page": 10,
            "text": "- Use when: Conversation is completed (order placed, support ticket \ncreated, information delivered), User chooses to stop (No thanks, \ncancel), or After final feedback fallback. \n \nImportant Tips \n- Always end long flows properly \u2014 don't leave paths hanging \n- Use clear End Reasons for reporting \n- Add a friendly End Message for better user experience \n- Don't put this in the middle of a flow unless you truly want it to \nstop there \n \nCENTER CANVAS \u2014 Flow Builder Area \nThis is where you visually build the journey. \n \nStarting Step (Message Keyword) \nKeywords shown: hello, hi, start \nWhen a user sends any of these, the flow begins. \n \nHow to add next steps \n1. Hover over the green dot under a node \n2. Drag from it \n3. Drop and choose the next node (message, input, condition, etc.)"
          },
          {
            "page": 10,
            "text": "Use these when you want the user to reply with data. \n \nOPERATIONS (Actions behind the scenes) \n- Send Email \u2014 Notify someone via email \n- Collect Payment \u2014 Take payment (Razorpay etc.) \n- Set Stage \u2014 Move contact in CRM/Kanban \nThese don't message the user \u2014 they perform actions. \n \nLOGIC & CONTROL (Smart decisions) \n- Condition \u2014 Create branches (IF/ELSE logic) \n- HTTP Request \u2014 Connect to external APIs \n- Set Tag \u2014 Add/remove tags for contacts \nThis is how your flow becomes intelligent. \n \nFlow Control \n- This node terminates the automation. Once the flow reaches this step. \n- Think of it like \"EXIT\" or \"CONVERSATION CLOSED\" \n- Use when: Conversation is completed (order placed, support ticket \ncreated, information delivered), User chooses to stop (No thanks,"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "pdf_names": [
      "Getting_Started_Dashboard_Overview (1).pdf"
    ]
  },
