      {
        "question": "what happens if my payment fails?",
        "answer": "If your payment method fails, Meta will suspend outbound messaging from your phone number, and you will receive an email alert from Meta. You must then update the payment method and clear any outstanding balance.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "page": 2,
            "text": "Meta bills you directly for every template message delivered through the WhatsApp \nBusiness API. Without a valid payment method on file, your phone numbers may be \ndeactivated and you will be unable to send or receive messages. This applies even if you \nare using WeNext \u2014 Meta\u2019s charges come directly to you, not through WeNext. \n3.2  How do I add a payment method in Meta? \n5.Log in to business.facebook.com \n6.Go to Settings > Payment Settings \n7.Click \u201cAdd Payment Method\u201d \n8.Select your country (India), choose credit or debit card \n9.Enter card details and click Save \n3.3  What happens if my payment method fails? \n\u2022Meta suspends outbound messaging from your phone number \n\u2022You receive an email alert from Meta \n\u2022You must update the payment method and clear any outstanding balance"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "if Meta requires additional review. Indian businesses with GST certificates usually get approved \nfaster. \n2.4  What happens if verification is rejected? \n\u2022Meta sends an email explaining the reason \n\u2022You can resubmit with corrected documents immediately \n\u2022Common rejection reasons: name mismatch, document too old (must be within 6 \nmonths), document not in English (add a certified translation) \n2.5  Do I need verification to start testing? \nNo. Without verification, your account operates at Tier 0 and can send up to 250 messages per \nday to any WhatsApp number. This is sufficient for testing. However, you cannot send OTP/\nauthentication templates and cannot scale beyond 250 messages without completing \nverification. \n3. Payment Method \u2014 Why It Is Mandatory"
          },
          {
            "page": 9,
            "text": "delivered messages across your templates before activating flows. This gives your \naccount the messaging history and quality signal Meta requires. \nQ: Can I use a virtual or VoIP number for WhatsApp API? \nA: Yes, as long as the number can receive an SMS or voice call during the one-time OTP \nverification process. After verification, the number does not need to receive calls. \nQ: What happens if a user blocks my number? \nA: That user can no longer receive your messages. Meta also records the block as a \nnegative quality signal. Too many blocks lower your quality rating and prevent tier \nupgrades. This is why sending relevant, opted-in messages is critical. \nQ: Is there a free tier for WhatsApp API? \nA: There is no traditional free tier, but you get free messaging in specific windows:"
          },
          {
            "page": 1,
            "text": "2.1  What is Business Verification? \nBusiness Verification is Meta\u2019s process of confirming that your business is a legitimate, \nregistered entity. It is mandatory to unlock higher messaging tiers, send certain template \ncategories, and use authentication templates (OTPs). \n2.2  What documents does Meta accept for verification? \n\u2022GST registration certificate \n\u2022Certificate of Incorporation \n\u2022Business license or trade license \n\u2022Utility bill in the business name (electricity, phone, water) \n\u2022Bank statement showing business name \n2.3  How long does verification take? \nTypically 2\u20135 business days. It can take up to 14 days if documents are unclear, incomplete, or \nif Meta requires additional review. Indian businesses with GST certificates usually get approved \nfaster."
          }
        ]
