        "answer": "The context provided covers the following topics:\n\n1. **Self-Attention**: A mechanism that allows every word in a sentence to look at every other word and decide how much to \"pay attention\" to it when building its own meaning.\n2. **Multi-Head Attention**: Running several attention computations in parallel.\n3. **Challenges**: Cost, latency, and context limits of large models.\n4. **Future Directions (What's Next)**: Four directions shaping the future of LLMs, including:\n\t* **Multimodal**: Unifying text, image, audio, and video understanding in a single model.\n\t* **Agentic AI**: Autonomous task execution and planning.\n5. **Transformer Architecture**: An overview of how text flows through a transformer model, including:\n\t* **Tokenization & Embeddings**\n\t* **Transformer Blocks**: Repeatedly refining the model's understanding.\n6. **Origins of the Transformer**: Introduced in a 2017 paper titled \"Attention Is All You Need\".\n7. **Model Training**: Trained on trillions of tokens of text with billions of parameters, allowing the model to implicitly absorb grammar, facts, reasoning patterns, and coding conventions.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "source": "LLM.pdf",
            "page": 5,
            "text": "6 \n3.2 Self-Attention \u2014 \"Who Is This Word Talking To?\" \nSelf-attention is the mechanism that lets every word in a sentence look at every other word and decide \nhow much to \"pay attention\" to it when building its own meaning. In the sentence \"The trophy didn't fit \nin the suitcase because it was too big,\" attention is what allows the model to correctly link \"it\" to \n\"trophy\" rather than \"suitcase\" \u2014 by weighing the relevance of every other word in context. \nPlain-English version \nAttention is a dynamic, learned weighting system \u2014 for every word, it asks \"which other words in this \nsentence matter most to understanding me?\" and blends their information in accordingly. \n3.3 Multi-Head Attention \nRather than computing attention once, the model runs several attention computations in parallel"
          },
