            "text": "outdated or invented. A response can be fluent and even factually correct in general and still be \nungrounded, meaning it wasn't really derived from what was retrieved. This is improved by prompting \nthe model to answer only from the provided context and say so when context is insufficient, attaching \ncitations to each claim, and running an automated check that compares the answer against the \nretrieved chunks. \nAnswer relevance is a separate axis again: an answer can be perfectly grounded in the retrieved text \nand still fail to address what the user actually asked, for example answering a related but different \nquestion. This is typically measured by comparing the semantic similarity of the generated answer back \nto the original query. \nWhy these metrics matter together"
